dAImon Keeper
=============

dAImon Keeper is a free, open-source reimplementation of Bullfrog Productions'
Dungeon Keeper. It is derived from KeeperFX.

It is not the original game and contains none of its data: a purchased copy of
the original Dungeon Keeper data files (CD, GOG, Steam or EA edition) is
required to play. Dungeon Keeper is a trademark of Electronic Arts. The
original game was made by Bullfrog Productions. This project is not
affiliated with or endorsed by Electronic Arts or Bullfrog Productions.


Based on KeeperFX
-----------------

This program is derived from KeeperFX (Dungeon Keeper Fan eXpansion),
https://github.com/dkfans/keeperfx, copyright (C) the KeeperFX Team and
contributors, and is distributed under the same licence (see "Licences"
below). It is not affiliated with the KeeperFX project.

This version has been extensively modified from KeeperFX: the source has been
reorganised into layered libraries, ported to SDL3 and native Linux, and
extended (in-game level and content editor, Vulkan renderer, ImGui interface,
external/AI player seats, and more). The git history of this project,
https://github.com/edorien/daimonkeeper, records every change and its
date. The copyright and author notices in the individual source files are
kept as they were.

Upstream base: KeeperFX master merged up to commit 225d19d44 (2026-10-03).
Content compatibility: campaigns and map packs made for KeeperFX 1.4
("KFX 1.4" in the version label).

Contributors to dAImon Keeper: see the git history.


Bundled campaigns and maps
--------------------------

The campaigns, map packs and levels shipped with this game (campgns/,
levels/, and their texts in lang/) are community-made content distributed
with KeeperFX. They remain the work of their authors, who are credited in
each campaign's own credits (in-game: main menu > Credits) and in the files
themselves.


